1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,225
The Carnival of Blood: a travelling show where some visitors never make it home.

2
00:00:04,445 --> 00:00:06,195
Here's how the location plays.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,499
Set the three Item Trap cards aside and shuffle the other Items.

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:15,288
Deal three face-down decks of two Items, add one Item Trap to each, and shuffle each

5
00:00:15,288 --> 00:00:17,844
deck. Then put one Item face up on top of each.

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:21,326
There are two kinds of trap here. First, Item Traps:

7
00:00:21,326 --> 00:00:25,365
one is hidden somewhere in each Item deck, and you only find them by searching.

8
00:00:25,585 --> 00:00:29,646
If a successful search draws an Item Trap, you must resolve it, unless something

9
00:00:29,646 --> 00:00:31,473
protects you, like Zappo the monkey.

10
00:00:31,693 --> 00:00:36,175
If the same search also found an Item, you can still keep the Item, but resolve the

11
00:00:36,175 --> 00:00:40,440
trap first. Item Traps are discarded afterwards unless the card says otherwise.

12
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:44,834
For example, the Hidden Cobra trap stays next to your Final Girl card.

13
00:00:44,834 --> 00:00:49,013
It hurts you every Upkeep, and the next time you would recover health, you discard

14
00:00:49,013 --> 00:00:50,440
the trap instead of healing.

15
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:55,425
Second, Terror Traps. Three of the location's Terror cards are traps, drawn in the

16
00:00:55,425 --> 00:00:57,453
Killer phase like any other Terror card.

17
00:00:57,673 --> 00:01:01,323
When one tells you to place its Trap token, put it in your current space.

18
00:01:01,323 --> 00:01:04,223
It goes off immediately, on you and on every Victim there.

19
00:01:04,443 --> 00:01:07,796
Victims are always killed. What it does to you depends on the trap.

20
00:01:07,796 --> 00:01:10,949
Then finish resolving the Terror card and discard it as normal.

21
00:01:11,767 --> 00:01:13,962
The Terror Trap reference card lists them.

22
00:01:13,962 --> 00:01:16,993
The Rope Trap makes you discard one Action card at random.

23
00:01:17,213 --> 00:01:20,002
The Spinning Floor Blade trap makes you roll two dice:

24
00:01:20,002 --> 00:01:24,083
each one to four does one damage, and each five or six lets you move one space.

25
00:01:24,303 --> 00:01:28,057
And the Acid Pitfall hurts you straight away, as shown on the reference card.

26
00:01:28,867 --> 00:01:32,984
Trap tokens are never discarded. They stay on the board for the rest of the game.

27
00:01:33,204 --> 00:01:37,765
Every time you, or a Victim, enter or are in a space with a Trap token, it goes off

28
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:40,457
again. Victims are killed; you suffer its effect.

29
00:01:40,677 --> 00:01:44,327
Enemies are never affected by traps, so the Killer walks straight through them.

30
00:01:44,327 --> 00:01:47,376
Plan your routes, and your Victims' routes, around trapped spaces.

31
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:51,827
A few tips. Zappo the monkey or Asami let you avoid Item Traps.

32
00:01:52,047 --> 00:01:55,631
Charlie can trade health for big Critical Blows once she's made her rescues.

33
00:01:55,851 --> 00:02:00,108
It's one of the hardest locations in logged games, so map where the Trap tokens

34
00:02:00,108 --> 00:02:00,971
land. Good luck.

